   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Adjectives agree",
     "texto": [
      "When it goes directly with a noun, the adjective usually comes before it and agrees with it in gender and number. Masculine: -ый, -ий or -ой; feminine: -ая/-яя; neuter: -ое/-ее; plural: -ые/-ие. Compare: новый дом, синяя сумка (blue bag), синее море (blue sea), новые книги.",
      "Some masculine nouns for people end in **-а/-я**. **Дедушка** is masculine, so we say **мой дедушка старый**.",
      "**новый** дом (new house), **новая** машина (new car), **новое** окно (new window), **новые** книги (new books)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
